        "original_id": "5ddd934b-16c2-570b-b023-c42413229497",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Cullen\n- Products: Punchlines, Eye Guess\n- Topics: American game shows, reboots, television hosting\n\nFacts:\n- Eye Guess was an American game show that originally ran from 1966 to 1969.\n- A 1979 American game show pilot titled Punchlines was a reboot of Eye Guess.\n- Bill Cullen hosted the failed 1979 American game show pilot Punchlines.\n- Bill Cullen was best known as a game show host during his career.\n- Bill Cullen hosted 23 shows over the course of his career.\n- Bill Cullen earned the nickname \"Dean of Game Show Hosts.\"\n- The later show Punchlines was based on the failed 1979 American game show pilot of the same name.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
